@startuml SeqNavigation
title Sequence Diagram — Navigation with OpenRouteService Proxy

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam dpi 180
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 160
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderThickness 1.5

actor       "Driver"               as DRIVER
participant "StationCard"          as CARD
participant "NavigationViewModel"  as VM
participant "RouteRepository"      as REPO
participant "Backend Server"       as BACKEND
participant "OpenRouteService"     as ORS
participant "NavigationScreen"     as NAV

== Step 1: Route Request ==

DRIVER -> CARD    : Tap "Navigate" button
CARD   -> VM      : loadRoute(startLat, startLng,\ndestLat, destLng)
VM     -> VM      : Set state = Loading
VM     -> REPO    : getRoute(start, destination)
REPO   -> BACKEND : GET /api/app/route\n?start=lng,lat&end=lng,lat

== Step 2: ORS Proxy ==

BACKEND -> ORS    : Forward request to ORS API\n(server-side API key)

alt ORS responds within 15 seconds
  ORS --> BACKEND : GeoJSON FeatureCollection\n(geometry + steps)
  BACKEND --> REPO : Relay GeoJSON response

  == Step 3: Route Parsing ==

  REPO -> REPO    : Parse GeoJSON →\nList<GeoPoint> + List<NavStep>
  REPO --> VM     : Result.success(RouteResult)
  VM   -> VM      : Set state = Success\n(polyline + stepList)
  VM   --> NAV    : Emit route state

  == Step 4: Navigation Display ==

  DRIVER -> NAV   : NavigationScreen opens
  NAV    -> NAV   : Draw route polyline\non OSMDroid map
  NAV    -> NAV   : Display first instruction\n(distance + maneuver)

  == Step 5: Step-by-Step Progression ==

  loop Driver advances along route
    DRIVER -> NAV : Tap "Next Step"
    NAV    -> VM  : nextStep()
    VM     -> VM  : Increment step index
    VM    --> NAV : Emit updated step
    NAV    -> NAV : Update instruction panel
  end

  DRIVER -> NAV   : Arrive at station
  NAV    -> VM    : Route complete
  VM    --> NAV   : Clear navigation state

else ORS timeout or error
  ORS --> BACKEND : Timeout / error
  BACKEND --> REPO : HTTP 502 / 504
  REPO --> VM     : Result.failure(exception)
  VM   -> VM      : Set state = Error
  VM  --> NAV     : Show error message to driver
end

@enduml
